1   = Verlet:      Verlet distance for optimization
linear  = contact law  Contact law, right now only hertz and linear
1       = RenderVideo: 1 if video should be render, 0 otherwise
2.0e5 = Kn:          Normal stiffness
57142.9  = Kt:          Tangential stiffness
190.9859    = Gn:          Normal dissipative coefficient
54.5674 = Gt:          Tangential dissipative coefficient
0.3    = Mu0:         Microscopic friction coefficient
0.0    = Beta:        Rolling stiffness coefficient (only for spheres)
0.0     = Eta:         Plastic moment coefficient (only for spheres, 0 if rolling resistance is not used)
4e-5   = dt:          Time step
4e-5 = dtOut:       Time step for output
1 = rho;
0.5 = Radius;
2 = applied vel x
4e-2 = tf
-0.75 = x1
0.0 = y1
0.7071 = z1
0 = x2
0 = y2
0 = z2
2 = sphere Coulomb mode: 0 elastic cap + dashpot always, 1 elastic cap + dashpot off sliding, 2 total tangential force cap + dashpot always
1 = tensile cutoff: 1 yes, 0 no
1 = integration scheme: 1 velocity verlet, 0 position verlet
0 = first contact correction: 1 yes, 0 no
